      "tabname": "Details",
      "class": "DepictionStackView",
      "views": [
        {
          "class": "DepictionMarkdownView",
          "markdown": "Dopamine greys out its Jailbreak button when the phone is already jailbroken. **DoubleDose** removes that lock inside a **duplicated** Dopamine, so you can press Jailbreak a second time and see what happens.",
          "useSpacing": true
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionSeparatorView"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionHeaderView",
          "title": "Read this first"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionMarkdownView",
          "markdown": "- Jailbreaking twice will most likely **kernel panic and reboot** the phone into a non-jailbroken state. It does not give you a second jailbreak.\n- It cannot boot loop the phone: Dopamine does not survive a reboot. Just jailbreak again afterwards.\n- Save anything you have open before you press the button.",
          "useSpacing": true
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionSeparatorView"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionHeaderView",
          "title": "How to use"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionMarkdownView",
          "markdown": "1. Jailbreak normally with your main Dopamine.\n2. Install DoubleDose, then fully close the duplicated Dopamine.\n3. Open the duplicate. Its Jailbreak button is now unlocked.",
          "useSpacing": true
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionSeparatorView"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionHeaderView",
          "title": "What it leaves alone"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionMarkdownView",
          "markdown": "- The Dopamine that did the jailbreak (Dopamine never loads tweaks into it).\n- Trollamine.\n- Everything else: it only loads into apps whose program is named Dopamine.\n\nTurn it off any time in Settings > DoubleDose.",
          "useSpacing": true
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionSeparatorView"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionHeaderView",
